These POST to `/api/owners`, then GET `/api/owners/{id}` and assert on `$.membershipTier`. Note `ownerNode()` (AcceptanceBase lines 117-125) produces a unique owner with **no email**, driving the BRONZE case; the SILVER case adds an email and uses a shared last name "solotier" (still unique here, so `namesakeCount` stays 0). The base class comment at `AcceptanceBase.java:85` notes uniqueness keeps `namesakeCount` at 0.

No test currently asserts on `namesakeCount` directly.

